mstory3Dll: fn_1_16924 returns whether the final ranking is left, on MPT_PC
Applied in order by runtimes/gc_wii/mp4/CMakeLists.txt with `git apply`.

The party's final ranking (mstory3Dll event 1, result.c) loops in fn_1_17DC0 until fn_1_16924
returns non-zero: START from the winner's pad, or 300 frames when the winner is a COM. Party Board
left that function without a return ("TODO PC return value"), so the value is undefined. In the
module it came back 0: the ranking went into the records view (fn_1_16AD4) and back, again and
again, and each round left a window behind. After 32 rounds, about 20,000 frames, HuWinCreate had
no window left, returned -1, and HuWinBGTPLvlSet read a null sprite member (seed 1's party autopilot,
M4-01, docs/titles/mp4.md section 21). The function now returns var_r31, the flag its two exits set,
which is what the caller tests.

